\end{equation}

If ${\mathcal{I}}({\mathfrak p}'') \ne L'$, then it follows that $s({\mathfrak p}'') < s(L')$.
By the covering property \eqref{eq-dis-freq-cover}, there exists a unique ${\mathfrak p}_{{\vartheta}}$ with
\begin{equation*}
